    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Ibaraki sits on the northern bank of the Yodo River, a key waterway that once powered Osaka’s early industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibaraki%2C_Osaka"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The city’s north‑south stretch is long and narrow, with the northern edge rising into the foothills of the Kinki mountains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibaraki%2C_Osaka"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Ibaraki is part of the sprawling Kyoto‑Osaka‑Kobe metropolitan area, blending suburban calm with urban accessibility.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibaraki%2C_Osaka"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Located in the Hokusetsu region of northern Osaka Prefecture, Ibaraki borders Kyoto’s Kameoka City to the north.",
